.TH hsh 1 "MAY 10, 2026" "1.0" "hsh (simple_shell) Man Page"

.SH NAME
.B simple_shell \- hsh
\- custom command line interpreter or shell

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.I (No options included as of this writing)

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a custom implementation of a simple UNIX shell. A minimalistic approach was taken in its design and implementation to provide the basic functions of a shell similar to the one designed by Ken Thompson. Design, compilation, and testing were conducted on Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.

.SH OVERVIEW
Similar to other command line interfaces, the simple_shell takes input from either the terminal or scripts and executes them as they appear. 

.SH INVOCATION
The GNU Compiler Collection,
.B gcc
, is recommended for compiling simple_shell with the following flags:
.P
.RS
.B $ gcc -Wall -Werror -Wextra -pedantic -std=gnu89 *.c -o hsh
.P
.RE
In **interactive mode**, the simple_shell displays a prompt ('$') and waits for user input. Commands are executed after pressing the Enter key.
.P
.RS
.B $ ./hsh
.br
($) /bin/ls
.P
.RE
In **non-interactive mode**, users can pipe commands or scripts into the shell.
.P
.RS
.B echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.RE

.SH BUILTINS
The following builtin commands are supported:
.TP
.B env
Prints all current environment variables.
.TP
.B exit
Exits the program and returns to the parent shell.

